/* Danish purpose strings (App Store PRD §3.9 / B3).

   The Info.plist value stays ENGLISH and is the fallback: "If a localized version of a key does not
   exist, the routines return the value stored in the Info.plist file."

   Guideline 5.1.1(ii) requires a purpose string to "clearly and completely describe your use of the
   data", so this must name WHERE the recording goes, not merely ask for the microphone. The failure
   mode for getting the key itself wrong is severe: an app that touches the microphone with no purpose
   string EXITS.

   `da` must also be listed in the Xcode project's knownRegions, or this .lproj is silently not built
   into the bundle and the English fallback ships to Danish iPads with nobody noticing. */

"NSMicrophoneUsageDescription" = "Børnelæring bruger kun mikrofonen i spillet \"Sig et Ord\", hvor barnet siger et dansk ord højt. Optagelsen sendes til Google Cloud Speech-to-Text for at genkende ordet og gemmes ikke. Mikrofonen er slået fra, indtil en voksen slår den til.";
